Carafe bench: the debug string flusher is stopped at exit. OutputDebugString starts a static std::jthread that
waits on a condition variable; at exit the jthread destructor requests a stop and joins, but nothing wakes the
condition variable, so Eden never exited once the software had printed a debug string (carafe-overlay prints
every line). The stop is requested under the mutex and the condition variable notified before the join.
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the file it changes.

diff --git a/src/core/hle/kernel/svc/svc_debug_string.cpp b/src/core/hle/kernel/svc/svc_debug_string.cpp
index c190fa7..22f4e5a 100644
--- a/src/core/hle/kernel/svc/svc_debug_string.cpp
+++ b/src/core/hle/kernel/svc/svc_debug_string.cpp
@@ -28,6 +28,17 @@ Result OutputDebugString(Core::System& system, u64 address, u64 len) {
         std::condition_variable msg_cv;
         std::chrono::steady_clock::time_point last_msg_time;
         std::optional<std::jthread> thread;
+
+        ~DebugFlusher() {
+            if (!thread) {
+                return;
+            }
+            {
+                std::lock_guard lock(msg_mutex);
+                thread->request_stop();
+            }
+            msg_cv.notify_all();
+        }
     } flusher_data;
     R_SUCCEED_IF(len == 0);
     // Only start the thread the very first time this function is called
